  {:namespace "re-frame.fresco" :var "error-boundary" :kind :var :facade? false :tier :advanced :owner "006"  :status "v1" :runtime-verified? true}
  ;; The two IN-TREE frame boundaries. Owner "002", not "006",
  ;; because the contract each realises — ENSURE at commit / SCOPE a live frame,
  ;; and the did-you-mean pair between them — is Spec 002's `frame-root` /
  ;; `frame-provider`, and Fresco's heads are shells over the same shared cores
  ;; the Reagent and UIx realisations use. `:tier :advanced` matches every other
  ;; `re-frame.fresco` row: Fresco is a substrate a consumer opts into, and its
