  ;; ---- The rest of the Fresco tree ------------------------------
  ;;
  ;; `implementation/fresco/src` is a `roster-covered-roots` entry, so every
  ;; namespace under it is classified: the five
  ;; OPTIONAL AUTHORING MODULES and the two TOOL-TIER namespaces below, plus
  ;; the door and `.server` above, with the eighteen `re-frame.fresco.impl.*`
  ;; namespaces recorded in the generator's `internal-namespaces`.
  ;;
  ;; They land HERE rather than in `jvm-namespaces` for the same reason
  ;; `.server` does: every one is `.cljs` (or, for `.native`, a `.cljc` whose
  ;; whole body is a `#?(:cljs …)` arm), so the JVM generator cannot require
  ;; them and `ns-publics` can never reach them.
  ;;
  ;; TIERS, and they follow each namespace's role rather than convenience.
  ;; The first five are genuine public authoring surfaces — each
  ;; carries a require-me-directly example in its own ns docstring, and
  ;; `substrate/adapter` is what an application passes to `(rf/init! …)`. So
  ;; `:advanced` throughout, matching the door's own rows (Fresco is an opt-in
  ;; published substrate, so it is not the front-porch set), except
  ;; `re-frame.fresco.substrate`, which is `:adapter` on exactly the footing
  ;; `re-frame.adapter.reagent` and `re-frame.adapter.uix` have. Those
  ;; tiers are docs-eligible, so `doc_api_check`'s coverage clause obliges
  ;; the five `docs/api/re-frame.fresco.*.md` pages. `^:no-doc` is NOT used
  ;; to make the gate quiet: a public
  ;; authoring surface with no documentation page is the friction this library
  ;; exists to remove.
