  ["re-frame.core" "reg-interceptor"]     {:tier :front-porch :owner "001" :status "EP-0022"
                                          :action :keep
                                          :justification "Front-porch: the public interceptor-authoring form (EP-0022). ->interceptor and ->interceptor* are not on the facade, so this is the one authoring door."}
  ;; There is no `reg-frame`: a frame is a LIVE runtime object, not a
  ;; program member, so a reg-* that constructed instead of registered would
  ;; corrupt the registrar grammar. `make-frame` (below) is the ONE
  ;; programmatic constructor; `frame-root` is the ENSURE mount recipe.
  ;; EP-0024: `make-frame` is the ONE frame constructor over the ONE
  ;; `frames` registry — it backs onto the unified `re-frame.live-frame/make-frame`,
  ;; RETURNS THE FRAME VALUE (the lifecycle token), and accepts BOTH
